            <ArticleTitle>Simultaneous thromboses of multiple coronary arteries in acute myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>240-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Simultaneous thrombotic occlusion of multiple coronary arteries in acute myocardial infarction is a well-recognised phenomenon. Studies have reported diffuse destabilisation of atherosclerotic plaques in patients with acute myocardial infarction, leading to the concept of &quot;pan-coronaritis&quot;. The putative mechanism is attributed to a systemic thrombophilic and inflammatory state. We report the occurrence of this phenomenon in two middle-aged male patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
